=== METHODOLOGY ===
1. PARTITIONING:
   Repository was partitioned into 16 size-balanced batches A01..D03 (see ADR-003, prompt 0001). Partition criteria: (a) keep packages whole, (b) target ~30 files per batch where possible, (c) split large packages (database, fsm, tesla) by sub-domain rather than alphabetically so each batch has a coherent review surface.

2. AUDITOR_DEPLOYMENT:
   Each of the 16 batches was audited by an INDEPENDENT general-purpose agent instance running model=claude-opus-4.7-xhigh (Claude Opus 4.7, Extra-high reasoning, internal-only). Agents had READ-ONLY tools (grep, glob, view). No agent could modify source.

3. CHECKLIST_APPLICATION:
   Every agent applied the same 15-item checklist (enumerated under AUDIT_SUMMARY.CATEGORY_COVERAGE_CHECKLIST_15). The checklist was provided verbatim in the agent prompt to ensure consistent coverage. Agents were instructed:
   - Cite file:line for every finding.
   - Classify severity HIGH/MED/LOW per the rubric below.
   - Suggest a concrete fix (not just "review this").
   - Skip duplicates within a batch (record the canonical site only).

4. SEVERITY_RUBRIC=
   HIGH = correctness bug, data-loss risk, panic risk, unbounded query, unit-mislabel that lies to the API consumer, missing context.WithTimeout on external call, goroutine without recover() that can crash the API binary.
   MED  = quality drift that does not currently misbehave but will (e.g., http.Error vs writeError envelope inconsistency, swallowed errors via `_ =`, missing pagination cap on a list endpoint that today returns small datasets, snake_case JSON tag drift, fmt.Sprintf into a query whose inputs are currently constants).
   LOW  = nits: dead code that the linter will flag, magic numbers in non-hot paths, log message style, doc gaps.

5. NORMALIZATION:
   All findings were dumped into a single `phase41_findings` table with columns: batch, file, line_start, line_end, category, severity, description, suggested_fix, deferred_to_phase. Triage decisions (next section) operate on this table.

6. PROMPT_GENERATION_RULES=
   - Each HIGH finding -> exactly one remediation prompt (1:1 mapping). Atomic = single source file + sibling _test.go.
   - Each MED-affected file -> one remediation prompt that fixes ALL MED findings in that file (1:N mapping by file). Atomic = single source file + sibling _test.go.
   - LOW findings -> NO prompts (rationale in TRIAGE section).
   - Prompt slot numbers are 4-digit zero-padded and gap-allocated to allow late-discovery insertions without renumbering.

=== TRIAGE ===
DECISIONS:

1. HIGH (85 findings) -> 85 remediation prompts, slot range 0010..0094.
   Rationale: HIGH findings are correctness bugs. Each one needs maximum revertibility (single git revert clears one bug). 1:1 prompt-to-finding gives the operator the finest possible rollback granularity.
   Examples in this bucket: missing context.WithTimeout on Tesla Fleet API client, snapshot-table reads that bypass SignalStore L1 layered live-state contract, signal_log queries with no time bound, unit-mislabel where a *_mi value is JSON-tagged distance_km, goroutines spawned without recover(), mutexes held across DB queries.

2. MEDIUM (417 findings across 211 files) -> 211 remediation prompts, slot range 5000..5210.
   Rationale: MED findings cluster by file (an aging handler tends to have 3-5 MED issues at once). Batching by file keeps the prompt count actionable (211 vs 417) without sacrificing atomic revertibility (one git revert clears all MED issues in one file). The 5000-block keeps MED prompts visually distinct from HIGH prompts in `ls -la logs/`.
   Examples in this bucket: writeError vs http.Error envelope inconsistency, missing %w wrap on returned errors, snake_case JSON tag drift, missing pagination cap on list endpoints, swallowed errors via `_ =`, fmt.Print* / log.Print* instead of zerolog.

3. LOW (299 findings) -> NO prompts generated. Recorded in phase41_findings for posterity.
   Rationale: LOW = nits, doc gaps, dead code that the compiler/golangci-lint will flag eventually. Promoting them to prompts would:
   (a) inflate the prompt slate from 299 actionable items to 598 mostly-noise items,
   (b) dilute signal-to-noise such that operators stop reading individual prompt logs,
   (c) compete with phase-42 prompt slots for operator attention,
   (d) duplicate work that lint/vet already does for free.
   The phase41_findings table preserves them so a future "lint sweep" prompt can grep them out.

DEFERRED_TO_PHASE_42:
   Findings in internal/tesla/**, internal/signal/**, internal/enums/** that overlap a pending phase-42 prompt (0066-0091 plus the 0080 tombstone) are tagged DEFERRED_PHASE_42 in phase41_findings and produce no phase-41 prompt. Operators should re-run the audit on those packages after phase-42 lands.

